<article class="env-definition" id="04IC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04IC">Definition <span data-tag="04IC">18.8.1</span>.</a> Let $f, g : (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C}) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}), \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D})$ be two morphisms of ringed topoi. A <em>2-morphism from $f$ to $g$</em> is given by a transformation of functors $t : f_* \to g_*$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ &  \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D} \ar[ld]_{f^\sharp } \ar[rd]^{g^\sharp } \\  f_*\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C} \ar[rr]^ t &  &  g_*\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C} }  \]
</div>
  <p> is commutative. </p>
</article>